{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 35, :comments ["<b>Vengeance and recompense are Mine.</b> [The word] is like \"indeed, the burning and the giving of taste\" [i.e., an infinitive used as a noun]; the meaning is: \"Vengeance is Mine and recompense is Mine, to repay them according to their deeds.\"" "<b>When their foot slips.</b> And the meaning is that they will fall and not be able to stand." "And the meaning of <b>לעת</b> is like \"and a wicked man for the day of evil\"; and it is a great sod." "<b>For it is near.</b> And let them not suppose that the vengeance will be upon their seed." "<b>And hasted things to come upon them.</b> [Either] וחש [means] each one of them hastens [regarding] the things to come, like בנות צעדה; or חש [is] a day [of] things to come. And the first is correct, and the word חש is from the [letters of] doubling [i.e., from the root with a doubled second letter]." "And the meaning of <b>עתידות</b>: the evils destined to come upon them."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {4 "The phrase בנות צעדה is obscure; rendered hyper-literally as it appears. The designation 'from the doubling' refers to חש being a geminate/second-letter-doubling root."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:26:14.134270415Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}